                        <div>
                            <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-base">The Non-Invasive Sensor Gap</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Hardware realities of Glucose and Hydration telemetry in 2026</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="space-y-3 text-xs text-slate-700">
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
                            <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm block mb-1">Continuous Glucose Monitoring (CGM)</span>
                            <p class="mb-2">Zero consumer smartwatches possess FDA clearance for optical/non-invasive blood glucose. Unvalidated optical wearables fail under motion/sweat artifacts.</p>
                            <span class="inline-block px-2 py-0.5 bg-teal-100 text-teal-800 font-semibold rounded text-[11px]">Production Solution:</span>
                            <p class="text-slate-600 mt-0.5">Must pair via BLE with minimally invasive ISF devices (e.g. Dexcom G7 direct-to-watch) and adjust for 5–10 min ISF-to-blood lag.</p>
                        </div>

                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-lg border border-slate-200">
                            <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm block mb-1">Wearable Hydration Modalities</span>
                            <p class="mb-2">Mass market smartwatches lack passive 24/7 continuous hydration sensors. Modalities split across four clinical categories:</p>
                            <ul class="list-disc pl-4 space-y-1 text-slate-600">
                                <li><strong>Spot Wrist BIA:</strong> Requires manual multi-finger electrode placement (Galaxy Watch 7).</li>
                                <li><strong>Sweat Biosensors:</strong> Requires active perspiration (Nix, Epicore microfluidic patches).</li>
                                <li><strong>Optical/Microwave:</strong> Hydrostasis Geca optical wristbands sensing 0.5–1% fluid shifts.</li>
                                <li><strong>BLE Smart Bottles:</strong> Weight/pressure pucks (HidrateSpark PRO 2) logging volume per sip.</li>
